<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 18.02 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 18.02 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 18.02 percent at auction on Tuesday from 20.04 percent at the last auction on April 29, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 6		Apr 29</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43KO708976     KZ43K31007978</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal)			2,216		1,260</p>
<p> Sold (nominal)			600		  600</p>
<p> Average price			 95.69 pct	  95.23</p>
<p> Average yield			 18.02		20.04</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Aug 7, 1997	July 31, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
